  "final_message": "The yen receipt test passes now, and the full suite is green (18/18).\n\n**Cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divided every amount by 100. JPY has no minor unit, so ¥500 was rendered as ¥5.00.\n\n**Fix:** I added a per-currency exponent table, with JPY at 0 and every other currency defaulting to 2. JPY now formats as `¥500` with no decimals, and GBP is unchanged (`£12.50`).\n\nBecause the helper is shared, cart totals and invoice lines in JPY get the same correction, not just receipts. No existing tests cover those paths, so I checked them by hand only through `formatMoney` itself.\n\nI haven't committed the change. Unknown currency codes still fall back to the old two-decimal behaviour (`XYZ 0.99`), which I left alone since you didn't ask about it.",
